{"authority":{"artifact":"CANDIDATE_IDENTITY_ONLY","data":"NONE","evidence":"DECLARED_LOCATORS_ONLY_NOT_VERIFIED","execution":"NONE","formation":"NONE","qualification":"NONE","results":"NONE"},"evaluation":{"holdout":"The 2024 interval is sealed and unread during proposal construction, parameter choice, implementation, and retrospective 2023 evaluation. Any read invalidates this proposal; no result is present here.","metrics":[{"id":"metric-1","statement":"Predeclared 2023 retrospective checks are pair-level net return after fixed costs, maximum drawdown, turnover, leg imbalance, repair incidence, and unresolved-state count; all are reject-only evidence, not Alpha."},{"id":"metric-2","statement":"Deflated Sharpe Ratio and Probability of Backtest Overfitting are reported only as multiple-testing rejection diagnostics over the four frozen coordinates and five feature configurations."},{"id":"metric-3","statement":"The primary coordinate is variant 0 with all features; every other coordinate and each one-feature deletion is secondary and cannot replace it after results are observed."}]},"evidence":[{"claim":"Cointegration provides a falsifiable long-run relation concept but does not establish that BTC and ETH are cointegrated.","id":"source-1-engle-granger","locator":"https://doi.org/10.2307/1913236"},{"claim":"Pairs trading supplies a historical relative-value design precedent, not evidence for this market, period, implementation, or profitability.","id":"source-2-gatev-nber","locator":"https://www.nber.org/papers/w7032"},{"claim":"The peer-reviewed Gatev publication is a declared research locator only and has not been verified by this proposal.","id":"source-3-gatev-rfs","locator":"https://doi.org/10.1093/rfs/hhj020"},{"claim":"Published cryptocurrency pairs research motivates a falsifiable BTC-ETH experiment but does not verify this hypothesis or its execution assumptions.","id":"source-4-crypto-pairs","locator":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ACCESS.2020.3024619"},{"claim":"Deflated Sharpe Ratio motivates a reject-only selection-bias diagnostic and is not a qualification threshold by itself.","id":"source-5-dsr","locator":"https://doi.org/10.3905/jpm.2014.40.5.094"},{"claim":"Probability of Backtest Overfitting motivates a reject-only multiple-testing diagnostic and is not a result claim.","id":"source-6-pbo","locator":"https://doi.org/10.21314/JCF.2016.322"}],"falsifiers":["2023 pair-level performance fails the predeclared cost, drawdown, leg-imbalance, repair-incidence, or unresolved-state limits.","Any coordinate, feature flag, threshold, pair, or evaluation rule is selected or changed after observing a result.","Any non-atomic two-leg outcome cannot be flattened by the single bounded repair or ends unresolved.","BTC and ETH completed M15 observations do not produce a finite positive ratio or a nonzero rolling variance.","The primary full-feature coordinate does not survive the predeclared DSR and PBO rejection diagnostics.","The sealed 2024 holdout is read before one-way admission and independently reproducible evaluation."],"hypothesis":"On frozen 2023 retrospective BTC and ETH M15/H1 inputs, an explicitly non-atomic, fixed-gross rolling close-ratio reversion rule with one bounded repair may produce falsifiable relative-value behavior across four predeclared coordinates; this proposal makes no stable-cointegration, Alpha, result, qualification, live, or atomic-fill claim and performs no pair search.","identity":"btc-eth-relative-value-2023-v1","inputs":{"channels":[{"id":"channel-1-btc-m15","statement":"Completed BTC M15 bars bound to bar channel 1 and executable handle 1."},{"id":"channel-2-eth-m15","statement":"Completed ETH M15 bars bound to bar channel 2 and executable handle 2."},{"id":"channel-3-btc-h1","statement":"Completed BTC H1 bars bound to bar channel 3; they are contextual and cannot issue handle 3 actions."},{"id":"channel-4-eth-h1","statement":"Completed ETH H1 bars bound to bar channel 4; they are contextual and cannot issue handle 3 actions."},{"id":"channel-5-snapshots","statement":"Each bar callback declares signed positions, pending-order quantities, and one bit-identical finite nonnegative shared USDT balance copy per executable."}]},"kind":"ResearchIntentProposal","non_claims":["NO_ALPHA_CLAIM","NO_DATA_AUTHORITY","NO_EVIDENCE_VERIFICATION","NO_EXECUTION_AUTHORITY","NO_FORMATION_AUTHORITY","NO_LIVE_AUTHORITY","NO_QUALIFICATION_AUTHORITY","NO_RESULT_AUTHORITY"],"parameter_space":{"parameters":[{"id":"parameter-1-coordinates","statement":"Exactly four frozen variants are allowed: (32,2.0,0.5,96), (32,2.5,0.5,96), (64,2.0,0.75,192), and (64,2.5,0.75,192) for lookback, entry z, convergence z, and maximum paired M15 holds."},{"id":"parameter-2-gross","statement":"Gross notional is fixed at 2000 USDT, split equally using the latest completed pair closes; no result-dependent sizing is admitted."},{"id":"parameter-3-features","statement":"The full feature set and exactly one deletion of H1 regime, rolling variance, convergence exit, or ETH-leg authority are frozen; deleting ETH-leg authority permits no entry rather than a single-leg substitute."},{"id":"parameter-4-selection","statement":"Variant 0 with all features is primary; no pair search, coordinate expansion, result fitting, 2024 read, or post-result replacement is admitted."}]},"revision":1,"schema_version":1}
